.TH EUCLID-CLI-EAM-CREATE-ACCOUNT 1 "August 2026" "euclid-cli 1.0.53" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-eam-create-account \- create a new Euclid account
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli
[\fB\-\-endpoint\fR \fIURL\fR]
.B eam create-account
.BR \-\-account\-id | \-a
.I ACCOUNTID
.BR \-\-name | \-n
.I NAME
[\fB\-\-description\fR|\fB\-d\fR \fIDESCRIPTION\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Creates a new account via the eam service's
.I create-account
action. The caller must be authenticated as a global administrator (see
.BR euclid-cli-eam-login (1)) -
unlike namespace and grant management, account creation is not delegable
to an account-scoped administrator.
.PP
An account is the top level of Euclid's access hierarchy: it owns a set of
namespaces (see
.BR euclid-cli-eam-create-namespace (1)),
and users are granted access to specific (account, namespace) pairs (see
.BR euclid-cli-eam-grant-namespace-access (1)).
.PP
The created account's JSON representation is printed to standard output.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-account\-id " " \fIACCOUNTID\fR
Account ID, unique across the deployment. Required.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-name " " \fINAME\fR
Human-readable account name. Required.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-description " " \fIDESCRIPTION\fR
Free-text description of the account's purpose. Defaults to an empty
string.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The account was created.
.TP
.B 1
Missing/invalid arguments, the request could not be sent, the caller is
not an authenticated global administrator, or an account with that
account ID already exists. If the failure was an expired or invalid
session (\fIHTTP 401\fR), the stored credentials file is removed; run
.B euclid-cli eam login
again before retrying.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 eam create-account \e
    --account-id 123456789012 --name "Payments Team" \e
    --description "Payments platform account"
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR euclid-cli-eam (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eam-login (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eam-list-accounts (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eam-delete-account (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eam-create-namespace (1)
